{"id":"000V6U","title":"Fortress Fillomino - Even Odds Can Be Useful (11x13)","author":"The Pi Guy","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-13T17:50:10+00:00","posted":"Heute, 16:45 Uhr","rules":"It’s a huge honour to be taking part in The Pedalling Pianist’s fantastic ‘Fortress Fillomino Fridays’ series. This was actually my first ever pencil puzzle so there was no small amount of pressure to get it right. Fortunately, I stumbled on the perfect rule for someone new to setting pencil puzzles and things quickly came together after that. So the rule for this week is PARITY LINES. Enjoy. :)\n\n[The eagle-eyed among you may also spot a few references to a certain date.]\n\nclick image to play this week's Fortress Fillomino\n\nFORTRESS FILLOMINO:\n\n• Divide the grid into orthogonally connected regions and fill each cell with a number (could be more than one digit) showing the number of cells in the region to which it belongs.\n\n• Each region must be either strictly larger than all of its orthogonal neighbours or strictly smaller than all of its orthogonal neighbours.\n\nPARITY LINES:\n\n• Each pair of cells along a parity line must consist of an odd and an even number.\n\n• The numbers on each individual parity line MUST NOT REPEAT.\n\nNote: For the answer check, enter the last digits only e.g. for a region of size 13, enter 3 instead.","solutionCode":"From top to bottom, the sizes of the regions in column 1 (e.g. 11, 13, 20, 26 -> 11132026). Only write each region size once per consecutive string of cells in the same region.","tags":["Fillomino"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/uummvftoqn","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/uummvftoqn","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":13,"cols":11,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-13T17:50:10+00:00"}